q4os-i18n (3.17.1-a1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  [ Q4OS Team ]
  * Version bump for public release build.
  * Synced q4os-tools/.pot_empty/update-manager.pot with q4os-updater's
    current source (two new msgids: "Hide details", added for the Plasma
    updater window's details-toggle button now actually reflecting its
    state; and the reworded Trinity-tray-icon-under-Plasma notice text,
    replacing the now-unused old wording). Propagated into all 174
    q4os-tools/<lang>/update-manager.po files via msgmerge -U (same
    mechanism as a_q4os/locales_update.sh) - existing translations
    preserved via msgmerge's own matching, only the changed/new msgids
    are now untranslated. This is a source-only, translator-facing sync:
    buildfs.sh already drops this package's own compiled
    update-manager.mo/um_config.mo before packaging (q4os-updater-common
    ships its own compiled catalogs instead), so no rebuild of this
    package is needed for this change to take effect anywhere.
  * Note for later: q4os-updater's own common/po/ (a curated 16-language
    subset, decoupled from this tree since q4os-updater commit bc879f7)
    was NOT touched here and still lacks these two strings - it needs its
    own separate sync before they'll actually show translated in a built
    q4os-updater-common/-plasma binary.
  * Refreshed q4os-tools/.pot_empty/q4os-screenscaler.pot against the
    package's current source (stale since 2019): the "Reset" button was
    retexted to "Defaults", and a new reset-confirmation dialog string
    ("Reset screen scaling configuration to system defaults now?") was
    added - 18 msgids total, up from 17. Propagated into all 174
    q4os-tools/<lang>/q4os-screenscaler.po files via msgmerge -U (same
    mechanism as a_q4os/locales_update.sh) - existing translations
    preserved via msgmerge's own matching, only the changed/new msgids
    are now untranslated (or fuzzy, for the reworded confirmation
    string).
  * q4os-screenscaler now compiles and ships its own q4os-screenscaler.mo
    directly (same /opt/trinity/share/locale/<lang>/LC_MESSAGES/ path
    this package used to install to), so buildfs.sh now drops this
    package's own copy to avoid a file conflict - same treatment
    update-manager/um_config already got. The .po source stays here for
    volunteers.
  * Filled in full q4os-screenscaler translations for id, ja, tr, uk and
    zh_CN (previously empty stubs here), matching the same 5 languages
    update-manager/um_config got filled in for previously - brings
    q4os-screenscaler's translated-language set in line with
    q4os-updater's own curated 16-language set.
  * Closed the remaining q4os-screenscaler translation gaps in the other
    11 languages (de es es_AR fr hu it nl pl pt pt_BR ru): "Defaults" was
    universally untranslated, and the reset-confirmation dialog string
    carried a stale fuzzy auto-match (missing the "now?" wording) that
    msgfmt was silently dropping from every one of these 11 - plus a few
    older pre-existing gaps (Designer-placeholder "Form (ui_form1)"/
    "Form1" in es/fr/pl, "Ruler [cm]:" in es, and two more stale fuzzy
    markers on already-correct pl translations). Every real string in
    all 16 bundled languages is now translated and non-fuzzy.
  * Added q4os-tools/.pot_empty/lookswitcher-trinity.pot (brand-new
    domain - lookswitcher-trinity has never had a .pot/.po here before,
    confirmed via git log --all) for the module's single translatable
    string, "Launching Look Switcher...". Propagated into all 174
    q4os-tools/<lang>/lookswitcher-trinity.po files (same "Creating"
    mechanism a_q4os/locales_update.sh uses for a new domain: copy the
    pot, set charset UTF-8 and Language: <code>); filled in real
    translations for the same 16-language curated set used by
    update-manager/q4os-screenscaler (de es es_AR fr hu id it ja nl pl pt
    pt_BR ru tr uk zh_CN), verified byte-identical to
    lookswitcher-trinity's own po/<lang>/lookswitcher-trinity.po; the
    other 158 language dirs are left as untranslated stubs for
    volunteers, matching the existing q4os-screenscaler.po pattern in
    minor language dirs.
  * lookswitcher-trinity now compiles and ships its own
    lookswitcher-trinity.mo directly (same /opt/trinity/share/locale/
    <lang>/LC_MESSAGES/ path), so buildfs.sh now drops this package's
    own copy to avoid a file conflict - same treatment update-manager/
    um_config/q4os-screenscaler already got. The .po source stays here
    for volunteers.
  * Fix: renamed q4os-tools/<lang>/q4os-screenscaler.po ->
    q4os_screenscaler.po and q4os-tools/<lang>/lookswitcher-trinity.po ->
    q4os_lookswitcher.po (plus the two .pot_empty templates), and updated
    buildfs.sh's drop lines to match. Both domains' bundled catalogs were
    being compiled and installed under the wrong name in their owning
    packages - TDE's KGenericFactoryBase::setupTranslations() looks up
    the catalog by the exact TDEInstance name given to each module's
    KGenericFactory (KcmScreenscalerConfigFactory("q4os_screenscaler"),
    KcmLookswitcherLauncherFactory("q4os_lookswitcher")), not the source/
    package name, and gettext catalog lookup is an exact filename match.
    Caught via a live-desktop screenshot showing lookswitcher-trinity's
    "Launching Look Switcher..." staying in English while the rest of a
    German desktop translated correctly. This package's own copies were
    already unused (dropped by buildfs.sh before packaging either way),
    so this is a rename-only, no-functional-change commit here - the
    actual runtime fix lives in q4os-screenscaler's and
    lookswitcher-trinity's own repos.

 -- Q4OS Team <devteam@q4os.org>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 19:08:38 +0000

q4os-i18n (3.16.3-a1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  [ Q4OS Team ]
  * q4os-updater-common now compiles and ships its own Trinity
    localization for the update-manager/um_config domains directly, at
    the same /opt/trinity/share/locale/<lang>/LC_MESSAGES/ path this
    package used to install to - so this package must stop shipping the
    same two files itself, or the two packages would fight over the same
    installed path. The q4os-tools/<lang>/{update-manager,um_config}.po
    sources themselves stay right here, alongside every other domain's -
    volunteers keep translating them in this same tree with Poedit, same
    as always (the coupling to q4os-updater was only ever by domain-name
    convention, never a build dependency, so nothing else changes for
    translators). Only the compiled .mo output for these two domains is
    now dropped before packaging (buildfs.sh, same treatment
    calamares-debian/q4os-shortcuts already got) - it would just be a
    duplicate of what q4os-updater-common now ships itself.
  * q4os-updater-plasma's 3 Qt5 binaries now also compile and ship their
    own translation catalogs (converted from these exact same
    q4os-tools/<lang>/{update-manager,um_config}.po files via lconvert at
    q4os-updater's own build time) - nothing new here for volunteers to
    learn or sync, the same .po sources now feed both toolkits.
  * Filled in full update-manager/um_config translations for ja, zh_CN,
    id, tr and uk (previously empty stubs here), matching the same new
    languages q4os-updater just added its own build side for.

